{
 "esm": "1.0.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "RadiationColumn",
  "description": "RRTM longwave radiation of the EqWeather reference suite (WRF ra_lw_physics = 1) assembled END-TO-END from the five stage components in components/atmospheric_radiation/rrtm_lw, mounted by reference as top-level systems and coupled in the RRTM order with variable_map/param_to_var edges (esm-spec 10.4): RRTMColumn (MM5ATM: extended column, column amounts, cloud optics) -> RRTMSetcoef (SETCOEF k-table coordinates) -> RRTMGasOptics (TAUGB1-16 optical depths and Planck fractions, GASABS quantisation) -> RTRNSweep (two-stream sweep, fluxes, HTR) -> RRTMLWHeating (flux divergence on the model column, glw, olr). Each stage keeps its `input_<x>` rewrite targets for standalone testing; in this document the mount-edge libraries (couplings/tests/rrtm_couple_*_inputs.esm) lower them to the stages' `<x>_in` coupling-target parameters, which the document's coupling fills from the upstream stage. The WRF column state enters RRTMColumn and RRTMLWHeating through dumped-profile libraries, so one document holds one column state (one regime). The Dudhia shortwave scheme (DudhiaSW) is co-mounted on the same column and the total radiative tendency rthraten = dthdt_lw + dthdt_sw is exposed, reproducing WRF's radiation_driver for ra_lw_physics = ra_sw_physics = 1. KNOWN BINDING LIMITATIONS (Rust CLI, EarthSciAST issue #198): the mounted components' own inline tests are re-run inside this document under the coupling and error, so run `./esm test --model RadiationColumn <this file>`; the leaves' index sets are redeclared at document level because a top-level ref mount does not merge them; a parent test cannot set a mounted component's parameter, so the shared scalars are prescribed in this model and coupled in.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "assembly",
   "coupling",
   "radiation",
   "rrtm",
   "wrf",
   "dudhia"
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "NLEV": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 59,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of model layers (WRF kte). Bound into the column grid at the import edge; 59 is the em_scm_xy reference column."
  },
  "NBUF": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 44,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of buffer layers MM5ATM adds above the model top, nint(p_top / (100 deltap)) with deltap = 4 hPa (RRTMINIT: NLAYERS = kme + nint(p_top*0.01/deltap) - 1); 44 for the reference column (p_top = 177.6 hPa)."
  },
  "NGPT": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 140,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of g-points after the 256-to-140 reduction."
  },
  "NBANDS": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 16,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Number of longwave bands."
  },
  "PLANCK_T0": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 159,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. TOTPLNK(i, band) holds the band Planck integral at T = PLANCK_T0 + i kelvin, i = 1..181 (RRTM's INDLEV = INT(T - 159.))."
  },
  "PLANCK_NODES": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 181,
   "description": "Declared at document level because the mounted leaves' index sets are redeclared here (a top-level ref mount does not merge the leaf's index_sets; EarthSciAST issue #198) and bound into every mount edge. Temperature nodes of the TOTPLNK table (160..340 K)."
  }
 },
